B.afn=new A.e5("Cervical plexus","Ventral rami of C1\u2013C4.","Formed deep to sternocleidomastoid; gives cutaneous branches at Erb\u2019s point and motor branches including ansa cervicalis; contributes to phrenic nerve.","Ansa cervicalis to infrahyoid muscles; segmental branches to prevertebral muscles; contribution to phrenic nerve.","Lesser occipital, great auricular, transverse cervical, supraclavicular nerves (cutaneous).","Variable sensory loss in neck/shoulder; phrenic involvement can affect diaphragmatic function if C3\u2013C5 pathways affected.",B.b3)
B.afm=new A.e5("Brachial plexus","Ventral rami of C5\u2013T1.","Roots \u2192 trunks \u2192 divisions \u2192 cords around axillary artery \u2192 terminal branches to upper limb.","Supplies all major motor innervation of upper limb via terminal branches.","Supplies most cutaneous sensation of upper limb via terminal branches and cutaneous nerves.","Upper trunk injury (Erb palsy) and lower trunk injury (Klumpke palsy) are classic patterns.",B.b3)
B.af2=new A.e5("Lumbar plexus","Ventral rami of L1\u2013L4.","Formed within psoas major; major branches include femoral and obturator; contributes to lumbosacral trunk.","Anterior thigh and medial thigh motor supply via major branches.","Anterior/medial thigh and parts of lower limb via femoral/obturator and cutaneous branches.","Can occur with pelvic/retroperitoneal pathology; patterns depend on affected branches.",B.b3)
B.afi=new A.e5("Sacral plexus","L4\u2013S4 (includes lumbosacral trunk L4\u2013L5).","Lies on pelvic surface of piriformis; gives sciatic nerve and other gluteal/perineal branches.","Motor to posterior thigh and most of leg/foot via sciatic; also gluteal muscles via gluteal nerves.","Posterior thigh (posterior femoral cutaneous) and much of leg/foot via terminal branches.","Lumbosacral plexopathy causes mixed motor/sensory deficits; may be due to trauma, tumors, or childbirth-related injury.",B.b3)
